####################################################################
# priority_rank.ttl — HAND-AUTHORED. NOT GENERATED.
#
# Asserts mda:priorityRank (declared in FRAMEWORK/ONTOLOGY/ontology.ttl) on
# each alarmprio:* concept. Kept out of vocab_generated.ttl deliberately:
# that file is mechanically regenerated from vocab_base.ttl + the annotated
# CSV on every build_framework.py run, and alarmprio:Hoog/Medium/Laag/Unknown
# are minted there per distinct CSV value with no room for a hand-authored
# extra fact to survive a rebuild. This file is a small, separate, stable
# layer over those same (stable, closed) four IRIs.
#
# Not loaded by CODE/evaluation_poc/op_knowledge.py's K.load_kb() — that
# pipeline is validated by CQ9-11 and the visualization and none of it needs
# a priority ordering. Loaded only by CODE/evaluation_poc/reasoner/assess.py,
# for CAT2a's "equal or higher priority" comparison.
#
# Ranking (higher = more urgent) is a domain-expert-settable default, not a
# derived fact — change the literals below if clinical practice disagrees.
####################################################################

@prefix mda:       <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#> .
@prefix alarmprio:  <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/alarm-priority/> .
@prefix xsd:        <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

alarmprio:Hoog     mda:priorityRank "3"^^xsd:integer .
alarmprio:Medium   mda:priorityRank "2"^^xsd:integer .
alarmprio:Laag     mda:priorityRank "1"^^xsd:integer .
alarmprio:Unknown  mda:priorityRank "0"^^xsd:integer .
